      "visual_observations": [
        "Initial text, table borders, GIFs, missing-image placeholders, fields and links are readable in all three modes.",
        "Down, Up and page-jump samples show coherent content movement and clean clipping at the viewport boundaries, without smeared GIFs, duplicated row fragments, border damage or page content painted into chrome.",
        "Missing-image ALT labels are shortened to fit their boxes; the displayed fragment stays inside the placeholder. Clipping of partially visible images/placeholders at the viewport edge is coherent.",
        "With bars hidden the content uses the exposed screen area. Inversion changes foreground/background consistently, including images and placeholders. Restored bars and focused input borders remain distinguishable.",
        "Focused-field scrolling does not visibly lose the focus outline or leave stale pixels in the inspected states."
      ],
